Step 6 of the build-up. Identical to virtualization-stacks-side-by-side-5.svg (see that prompt), with nothing
moved, plus everything that makes the point that the VMM is exchangeable:

- VirtualBox (KVM backend) as a third VMM in the Linux/KVM box, with its VM -
  the same product as box 2, but here it is only the user-space half.
- The subtitle "one hypervisor, many VMMs" and the note "the VMM is
  exchangeable - same hypervisor" for that box.
- The footer: with KVM the hypervisor is shared and the VMM is just a program,
  while VirtualBox and VMware ship both halves themselves.
